      "text": "To simplify the expression \\(\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i} + \\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i}\\), we start by finding a common denominator. The misalignment in the denominators indicates that we need to simplify each fraction first.\n\nFirst, simplify \\(\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i} \\cdot \\frac{3 + 5i}{3 + 5i} = \\frac{(3 + 5i)(3 + 5i)}{(3 - 5i)(3 + 5i)} = \\frac{(3 + 5i)^2}{(3)^2 - (5i)^2}.\n\\]\n\nCalculate the numerator and the denominator:\n\nNumerator:\n\\[\n(3 + 5i)^2 = 3^2 + 2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 5i + (5i)^2 = 9 + 30i + 25i^2 = 9 + 30i - 25 = -16 + 30i.\n\\]\n\nDenominator:\n\\[\n(3 - 5i)(3 + 5i) = 3^2 - (5i)^2 = 9 - 25i^2 = 9 + 25 = 34.\n\\]\n\nThus, we have:\n\\[\n\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i} = \\frac{-16 + 30i}{34} = \\frac{-16}{34} + \\frac{30i}{34} = -\\frac{8}{17} + \\frac{15i}{17}.\n\\]\n\nNow, simplify \\(\\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i} \\cdot \\frac{3 - 5i}{3 - 5i} = \\frac{(3 - 5i)(3 - 5i)}{(3)^2 + (5i)^2} = \\frac{(3 - 5i)^2}{9 + 25i^2}.\n\\]\n\nCalculate the numerator and the denominator:\n\nNumerator:\n\\[\n(3 - 5i)^2 = 3^2 - 2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 5i + (5i)^2 = 9 - 30i + 25i^2 = 9 - 30i - 25 = -16 - 30i.\n\\]\n\nDenominator:\n\\[\n(3 + 5i)(3 - 5i) = 3^2 - (5i)^2 = 9 - 25i^2 = 9 + 25 = 34.\n\\]\n\nThus, we have:\n\\[\n\\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i} = \\frac{-16 - 30i}{34} = \\frac{-16}{34} - \\frac{30i}{34} = -\\frac{8}{17} - \\frac{15i}{17}.\n\\]\n\nCombining the two simplified fractions:\n\\[\n-\\frac{8}{17} + \\frac{15i}{17} + \\left( -\\frac{8}{17} - \\frac{15i}{17} \\right) = -\\frac{8}{17} + \\frac{15i}{17} - \\frac{8}{17} - \\frac{15i}{17} = -\\frac{8}{17} - \\frac{8}{17} = -\\frac{16}{17}.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the simplified expression is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-\\frac{16}{17}}.\n\\]",
