      "text": "To simplify the expression \\(\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i} + \\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i}\\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. Simplify each fraction separately by multiplying the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator.\n2. Combine the simplified fractions.\n3. Simplify the resulting expression.\n\n### Step 1: Simplify \\(\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i}\\)\nMultiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator, which is \\(3 + 5i\\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i} \\cdot \\frac{3 + 5i}{3 + 5i} = \\frac{(3 + 5i)(3 + 5i)}{(3 - 5i)(3 + 5i)}\n\\]\n\nFirst, simplify the denominator using the difference of squares formula \\((a - b)(a + b) = a^2 - b^2\\):\n\n\\[\n(3 - 5i)(3 + 5i) = 3^2 - (5i)^2 = 9 - 25(-1) = 9 + 25 = 34\n\\]\n\nNext, simplify the numerator by expanding:\n\n\\[\n(3 + 5i)(3 + 5i) = 3^2 + 2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 5i + (5i)^2 = 9 + 30i + 25(-1) = 9 + 30i - 25 = -16 + 30i\n\\]\n\nSo, we have:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i} = \\frac{-16 + 30i}{34} = -\\frac{16}{34} + \\frac{30i}{34} = -\\frac{8}{17} + \\frac{15i}{17}\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Simplify \\(\\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i}\\)\nMultiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator, which is \\(3 - 5i\\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i} \\cdot \\frac{3 - 5i}{3 - 5i} = \\frac{(3 - 5i)(3 - 5i)}{(3 + 5i)(3 - 5i)}\n\\]\n\nFirst, simplify the denominator using the difference of squares formula:\n\n\\[\n(3 + 5i)(3 - 5i) = 3^2 - (5i)^2 = 9 - 25(-1) = 9 + 25 = 34\n\\]\n\nNext, simplify the numerator by expanding:\n\n\\[\n(3 - 5i)(3 - 5i) = 3^2 + 2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot (-5i) + (-5i)^2 = 9 + 30i + 25(-1) = 9 + 30i - 25 = -16 + 30i\n\\]\n\nSo, we have:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i} = \\frac{-16 + 30i}{34} = -\\frac{16}{34} + \\frac{30i}{34} = -\\frac{8}{17} + \\frac{15i}{17}\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Combine the simplified fractions\nWe now add the two simplified fractions:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i} + \\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i} = \\left( -\\frac{8}{17} + \\frac{15i}{17} \\right) + \\left( -\\frac{8}{17} + \\frac{15i}{17} \\right)\n\\]\n\nCombine the real and imaginary parts:\n\n\\[\n= -\\frac{8}{17} - \\frac{8}{17} + \\frac{15i}{17} + \\frac{15i}{17} = -\\frac{16}{17} + \\frac{30i}{17}\n\\]\n\nThus, the simplified form of the given expression is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-\\frac{16}{17} + \\frac{30i}{17}}\n\\]",
